    },
    {
      "id": "hUQTpVeoW4kzvaV8ShOoD",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 502.95885634426907,
      "y": 6629.843976695502,
      "width": 881.63134765625,
      "height": 60,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4e",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1650311941,
      "version": 545,
      "versionNonce": 1700536240,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1770016245459,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The problem we are trying to solve here is inventory fragmentations.\nUsers hold tickets locking the database row, but abandon the payment flow.\nWe have to release the seats promptly, the events appear sold out while valid seats appear idle in expired carts.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "The problem we are trying to solve here is inventory fragmentations.\nUsers hold tickets locking the database row, but abandon the payment flow.\nWe have to release the seats promptly, the events appear sold out while valid seats appear idle in expired carts.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Ji2abdlke91S_eB--W5Ud",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1504.958856344269,
      "y": 7419.343976695502,
      "width": 540.4315185546875,
      "height": 140,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4g",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1451145771,
      "version": 1262,
      "versionNonce": 1083798960,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1770016259128,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Step 1 : Passive expiration\nWe try just in time validation.\nWhen any user attempts to view or book a specific seat, the booking\nservice checks if the status is equal to reserved, and, if : \nexpires at < Time now,\nTransaction treats seat as available and immediately updates the \nexpiration time with : Time now + 10 mins",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Step 1 : Passive expiration\nWe try just in time validation.\nWhen any user attempts to view or book a specific seat, the booking\nservice checks if the status is equal to reserved, and, if : \nexpires at < Time now,\nTransaction treats seat as available and immediately updates the \nexpiration time with : Time now + 10 mins",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "6ystESJgCdhR4PJISG6jV",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1634.9588540792925,
      "y": 7588.343976695502,
      "width": 636.095458984375,
      "height": 340,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4h",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 884356325,
      "version": 1526,
      "versionNonce": 859783088,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1770016259128,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Step 2 : Active cleanup\n1. When a booking is created, Reservation Service adds a task to a \ndelay queue which can be implemented via \n- Redis Sorted Sets OR\n- Amazon SQS with a delivery delay, and scheduled for 10 min into future\n\n2. Cleanup worker polls the queue, and when the 10 min timer matures, \nit receives the booking id\n\n3. For reconciliation the worker checks the primary database. If the \nbooking status is still pending, the user never paid, it executes a roll back.\nIt does the rollback by updating the DB to available and update the \nRedis Seating cache by flipping the bit to zero.\n\n4. The CDN cache will eventually expire in a few seconds, and on the next fetch, \nthe CDN will pull this new zero state from Redis and update its cache. All users \nwill now see that seat turn green and become available",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Step 2 : Active cleanup\n1. When a booking is created, Reservation Service adds a task to a \ndelay queue which can be implemented via \n- Redis Sorted Sets OR\n- Amazon SQS with a delivery delay, and scheduled for 10 min into future\n\n2. Cleanup worker polls the queue, and when the 10 min timer matures, \nit receives the booking id\n\n3. For reconciliation the worker checks the primary database. If the \nbooking status is still pending, the user never paid, it executes a roll back.\nIt does the rollback by updating the DB to available and update the \nRedis Seating cache by flipping the bit to zero.\n\n4. The CDN cache will eventually expire in a few seconds, and on the next fetch, \nthe CDN will pull this new zero state from Redis and update its cache. All users \nwill now see that seat turn green and become available",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
